  "sourceFile": "Drive file id 1-MK6Ip3Hz_Et3258zOrM73HL5XM82m3I (\"712f20a8-....pdf\", TEC Cycle of Prayer folder); original diocesan source per Josh's own roster: https://www.episcopalct.org/news/download-the-2025-26-cycle-of-prayer/",
  "ingested": "2026-09-29",
  "notes": [
    "The source covers November 30, 2025 through November 22, 2026, with a final unpopulated row reading 'November 29, 2026: Advent 1 (a new Cycle of Prayer begins)' -- no parishes or ministries are actually listed for that date, so no entry is fabricated for it here. Only the weeks landing in calendar 2026 (January 4 through November 22) are otherwise in this file, per this corpus's existing cross-liturgical-year convention -- the 5 weeks in late 2025 are deferred to a future episcopal-connecticut-2025.json.",
    "April 5, 2026 (Easter) is deliberately absent from `entries`: the source replaces its normal three-parish/ministry-network row with a single seasonal reflection paragraph naming no specific parish, ministry, or category -- there is nothing to transcribe as a subject that week, not an oversight.",
    "The source's own fourth column ('Anglican Cycle of Prayer') reproduces the worldwide Anglican Communion Cycle of Prayer's province name for that week -- deliberately NOT re-transcribed into this file's `entries`, since that content is already the separate, dedicated scope-'communion' corpus (anglican-communion-2026.json) and duplicating it here would create two sources of truth for the same tier.",
    "Each week's 'ECCT Wider Witness & Ministries' column is kept as ONE category subject per week, verbatim, rather than split at its own internal semicolons/periods -- these read as continuous prose call-outs (sometimes with illustrative examples introduced by 'For...') rather than a clean parallel list the way, e.g., St. Bede's Day-31 ministries list does.",
    "Three parish names are unusual combined/yoked forms, preserved exactly as printed rather than guessed apart into two subjects: 'St. Peter's Grace, Monroe' (May 3), 'Good Shepherd/Immanuel St. James Chapel, Shelton' (August 2), and 'St. Peter's-Trinity, Thomaston' (September 27).",
    "August 16, 23, and 30 name Episcopal schools/seminaries/campus ministries, not congregations -- recorded as `category` subjects (full name plus city combined, since `category` has no separate place field) rather than `parish` subjects, consistent with how this corpus already treats schools elsewhere (e.g. episcopal-central-gulf-coast-2026.json's October 4 entry). August 30's 'Berkeley Divinity School; New Haven' is transcribed with a comma in place of the source's own semicolon, since every other entry in this list uses 'Name, City' and the semicolon here reads as a plain punctuation slip rather than a meaningful list boundary."
  ],
